<title>USA: Staples decision to be issued today.</title>
<headline>Staples decision to be issued today.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. District Judge Thomas Hogan will hand down his decision on the proposed $4 billion merger of Staples and Office Depot at 4.30 pm EDT (2030 GMT) today, a clerk of the court said Monday.  </p>
<p>The Federal Trade Commission has asked for the merger to be blocked, arguing that if the office supply superstores were to merge it would result in higher prices for consumers.</p>
<p>Lawyers for Staples and Office Depot told the court that the FTC failed to take into account competition from other firms which sell a more limited variety of office supplies and mail-order firms which have a wide variety of supplies.</p>
</text>
